# Custom domain for GitHub Pages
#
# The project owner should create a file named `CNAME` (no extension) in this
# `site/` folder containing ONLY their subdomain on a single line, for example:
#
#   mycel.example.com
#
# Then add a DNS CNAME record pointing that subdomain to <owner>.github.io and
# set the custom domain under Settings -> Pages. All site paths are relative,
# so the site works at the domain root or at <owner>.github.io/mycel/.
